 and familial changes that reshaped the lineage"}, "D3S1": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0236-665a24030949:d02", "start": 0, "end": 184, "text": "Walter Erskine, Earl of Mar and Kellie (1865–1955) Walter John Francis Erskine, 12th Earl of Mar and 14th Earl of Kellie, KT, JP (29 August 1865 – 3 June 1955) was a Scottish nobleman."}, "D3S2": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0236-665a24030949:d02", "start": 185, "end": 342, "text": "The eldest son of Walter Erskine, 11th Earl of Mar and Mary Anne Forbes, he was educated at Eton and served as a lieutenant in the Scots Guards from 1887-92."}, "D3S3": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0236-665a24030949:d02", "start": 343, "end": 482, "text": "He succeeded his father in 1888, and in 1892 married Lady Violet Ashley-Cooper, daughter of Anthony Ashley-Cooper, 8th Earl of Shaftesbury."}, "D3S4": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0236-665a24030949:d02", "start": 483, "end": 577, "text": "They had three children: He was a Scottish Representative Peer from 1892-1950, and held office"}, "D4S1": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0236-665a24030949:d03", "start": 0, "end": 24, "text": "14th Earl of Kellie [ S."}, "D4S2": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0236-665a24030949:d03", "start": 25, "end": 56, "text": ", 1619 ] on 16 September 1888 ."}, "D4S3": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0236-665a24030949:d03", "start": 57, "end": 103, "text": "1 He succeeded as the 14th Lord Dirletoun [ S."}, "D4S4": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0236-665a24030949:d03", "start": 104, "end": 135, "text": ", 1619 ] on 16 September 1888 ."}, "D4S5": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0236-665a24030949:d03", "start": 136, "end": 187, "text": "1 He succeeded as the 14th Viscount of Fentoun [ S."}, "D4S6": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0236-665a24030949:d03", "start": 188, "end": 219, "text": ", 1619 ] on 16 September 1888 ."}, "D4S7": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id"